bootforge/express-api/handlers/handler-b.instructions:
This handler is supposed to reject requests without an id — but valid AND invalid requests both come back 200. Fix it **without restructuring** (one keyword is missing).

```js
export function getItem(req, res) {
  if (!req.params.id) {
    res.status(400).json({ error: { code: 'BAD_REQUEST', message: 'id required' } });
  }
  res.status(200).json({ data: { id: req.params.id } });
}
```

*(Simulation convention: `req` is a plain object `{ method, path, params, query, body, headers }`; `res` is a recorder the tests provide — `statusCode` starts at 200, `body` starts undefined, and `status(code)` / `json(body)` each record their argument and return `res` so calls chain.)*

